docs {
  # Get product

  Returns one product with its category, description and every image. Backs
  the mobile product page; desktop can use it too. Related products are not
  included: ask `GET /api/v1/catalog?category=<slug>` for them, so a failure
  there costs a section rather than the product.

  The product comes from the external demo feed
  (`https://api.escuelajs.co/api/v1/products/{id}`), cached in process for
  **5 minutes** per id. Failures and unknown ids are never cached.

  ## Auth

  None. This endpoint is public.

  ## Parameters

  - `id` (path, integer, required) — the product's feed id. Plain digits,
    `1` or greater.

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK

  {
    "product": {
      "id": 4,
      "name": "Classic Grey Hooded Sweatshirt",
      "category": { "id": 1, "name": "Clothes", "slug": "clothes" },
      "priceAud": 90,
      "description": "Elevate your casual wear with this classic grey hooded sweatshirt.",
      "imageUrls": [
        "https://i.imgur.com/R2PN9Wq.jpeg",
        "https://i.imgur.com/IvxMPFr.jpeg"
      ]
    }
  }

  - `product.id` (number) — feed identifier.
  - `product.name` (string) — product name.
  - `product.category.id` (number|null), `.name` (string), `.slug` (string) —
    empty strings and null when the feed has no category.
  - `product.priceAud` (number) — price, assumed AUD (see `GET /api/v1/products`).
  - `product.description` (string) — empty when the feed has none.
  - `product.imageUrls` (string[]) — every image, feed order; may be empty.

  ### 400 Bad Request — invalid id

  The id is not plain digits, is 0, or is too large. The feed is not contacted.

  {
    "statusCode": 400,
    "error": "Bad Request",
    "message": "Product id must be a positive whole number.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/products/abc",
    "method": "GET"
  }

  ### 404 Not Found — unknown product

  {
    "statusCode": 404,
    "error": "Not Found",
    "message": "Product 999999 does not exist.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/products/999999",
    "method": "GET"
  }

  ### 502 Bad Gateway — catalogue source unavailable

  {
    "statusCode": 502,
    "error": "Bad Gateway",
    "message": "The product catalogue source is unavailable.",
    "validation": [],
    "url": "/api/v1/products/4",
    "method": "GET"
  }
}
